{# One block per input. The tag name IS the identifier the agent binds in its REPL and `type=` the
   runtime type, so the sentence below can refer to each input by the exact name the agent has.
   The blocks and that sentence are one surface — change them together. #}
{% for inp in inputs %}
<{{ inp.name }} type="{{ inp.type }}">
{{ inp.value }}
</{{ inp.name }}>
{% endfor %}
{% if inputs %}{% set names = inputs | map(attribute="name") | list %}{% set plural = names | length > 1 %}
The input variable{{ "s" if plural else "" }} `{{ names | join("`, `") }}` {{ "are" if plural else "is" }} available in your REPL with descriptions given above.
{% if subinvoke_description is not none %}{{ "They are" if plural else "It is" }} not automatically available to `invoke()` calls you make, so making {{ "them" if plural else "it" }} available to sub-invokes requires passing {{ "them" if plural else "it" }} explicitly.
{% endif %}{% endif %}
